---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="How the cards work"
  lang="en"
  description="How recitation cards work: surah breakdown, hizb markers and goal validation."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-600">Methodology</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink-900 dark:text-white">How the cards work</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-ink-600 dark:text-night-300">
      Each level's yearly goal is broken down by surah, themselves split into weekly goals. Each weekly goal
      matches a cell: if the section is correctly recited, the teacher writes the recitation date in it.
      Otherwise, the cell stays blank and a new deadline is set.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-600 dark:text-night-300">
      After two consecutive missed goals, a discussion is scheduled with the parents to understand and find a
      solution to the difficulty.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-ink-100 p-6 dark:border-night-800">
      <h2 class="font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">Hizb markers</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-600 dark:text-night-300">
        Hizb boundaries do not have a separate card: they are marked directly on the card, with a double border
        around the date cells that correspond to the start of a hizb. Students and teachers can therefore track
        progress both surah by surah and hizb by hizb, with a single card.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl bg-gold-50 p-8 dark:bg-night-900">
      <h3 class="font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">The card, in principle</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-600 dark:text-night-300">
        A card is assigned to each student and corresponds to a level. It is personalised: name, class, teacher,
        level and yearly goal are listed on it. The student always keeps it and presents it to their teacher at
        every recitation; the teacher keeps a duplicate.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a href="/en/methodology/levels" class="mt-12 inline-block text-sm font-semibold text-gold-600 hover:underline">
      ← See the levels in detail
    </a>
  </section>
</Layout>
